members.description:
U5 [CC0EBB59 / C29EBEE5] Operator docs, the marker contract. Contract rewritten to the option A plan text at the 173-F harvest (2026-09-29, plan Harvest Checklist step 5); supersedes the pre-option-A contract ("non-empty => claim-activated" is WITHDRAWN). Source: docs/exec-plans/2026-09-13-shipment-claim-scheduler-reconciliation-plan.md (U5, attempt 7) and docs/decisions/2026-09-28-173f-marker-lifecycle-option-a-decision.md. Wave 5 of the 154-S bootstrap slice.

Domain: docs. File: docs/design-docs/scheduler-baseline-marker-contract.md (new, hand-written). Generated docs/cli-reference/* is not edited. Depends on U0b (173.007-T), U1 (173.001-T) and U3 (173.003-T) (the dependency on the retired U2 was removed; U4 is deferred — see the verification-status column).

Publish:
* the pinned key scheduler_baseline_claim and value shape (activating shipment ID, non-empty string); reserved but not write-protected;
* a stability note: contract version scheduler-baseline-marker/v1; any change to key, value shape or predicate is a breaking change needing a new version and a consumer notice;
* the copy-pasteable read recipe with EXACT JSON paths (the same paths U0b asserts): (1) active shipment: backlogit shipment list --status active --format json (or MCP backlogit_list_shipments {"status":"active"}) returns a JSON array — length 0 => no item is claim-activated; length > 1 => indeterminate, fail closed; length 1 => shipment ID is .[0].id; (2) manifest: .[0].custom_fields.items[] (there is NO top-level items); (3) each item: backlogit get <id> --format json or MCP backlogit_get_item, reading .status and .custom_fields.scheduler_baseline_claim;
* the three-part option A predicate (normative), verbatim from the decision artifact: claim-activated iff status == active AND the marker == the ID of the currently active shipment AND the item is in that shipment's current items manifest; "non-empty => claim-activated" explicitly withdrawn;
* the marker is advisory; the backlogit claim gate is authoritative;
* the option A lifecycle table with a verification-status column: claim write and re-claim overwrite (incl. stale foreign value) verified by U0a; removed by rollback (in-process and journal) verified by U3 and U0c; marker-only write on an already-active member-parent unaudited (no event); kept through block, unblock, return, ship, abandon, normalize and generic update/move by construction (code-cited), with the regression net tracked by the follow-on feature's U4 task named by ID (182.001-T under 182-F) — consumers read that task's status, so the row never needs a later edit;
* residuals R1-R3, text identical to the decision artifact; R3 published as the split rule: transport side effects (every CLI read and MCP server startup open a recovering workspace via core.NewWorkspace; strictly read-only consumers use an already-running MCP server they did not start); the consumer rule (read disagreement, a pending claim journal under <storage-root>/ops/ (detect with backlogit doctor), a doctor journal finding, >1 active shipment, any non-zero exit/error from a recipe read — in particular "open workspace: recover shipment operations" — or any MCP tool error means indeterminate, defer to the claim gate; a consumer never invokes a lifecycle command; a re-read whose shipment ID or manifest differs from the first read is indeterminate; MCP results are JSON text content parsed before the paths apply; a missing custom_fields or key means "not marked"); the operator-only remediation (fresh-process CLI backlogit sync, then backlogit_sync_index if an MCP server is running; on recovery error, backlogit doctor and escalate);
* the mixed-binary caveat: ANY binary that opens the workspace (CLI or MCP server, including one a consumer invokes or starts) must include U1b;
* the autoharness consumer should not treat the contract as operative before the rollout checkpoint is recorded (docs/compound/workflow-issues/stable-contract-before-two-agent-adoption-2026-04-05.md);
* SQL query is secondary (json_extract); full defect resolution needs the autoharness follow-up.

AC: the doc contains every item above; the predicate and residual text match the decision artifact verbatim; the recipe JSON paths are identical to the paths U0b (1) and (2) assert.
